edukasaun-desktop-menu (0.11.0~rc2) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Release candidate 2 of 0.11, close to the final stable version.
  * Eduka-Settings opens on "All Settings": an overview of every setting
    with a search box, in sections like the system settings of a full
    desktop (Appearance, Eduka, Preferences, Hardware, Administration).
    Tiles open Eduka pages or the LXQt/Debian tool for display, network,
    sound, Bluetooth, printers, power, disks, input method, startup
    applications, preferred applications, windows, firewall and software
    sources (only tools that are installed are shown).
  * Users (new): add and delete accounts (with or without their files),
    full name, login name (home folder, AccountsService and login lists
    follow), password (own password with the current one), standard or
    administrator, can log in, shown on the login screen, and the account
    picture (photo, initials or a Noto Emoji picture) for SDDM, LightDM
    and Eduka-Desktop through AccountsService and ~/.face. Root helper
    eduka-users-apply (polkit org.edukasaun.desktop.users) checks every
    value and keeps the last administrator.
  * Fonts (new, Appearance → Fonts): default, desktop, document, monospace
    and window title fonts, text scaling factor, hinting, antialiasing and
    subpixel order for Qt/LXQt, GTK 2/3/4, the GNOME keys, fontconfig, X
    resources, pcmanfm-qt, Openbox and xfwm4 (eduka_fonts.py).
  * Date & Time (new) and Sync time in the Action Center: network time,
    "Sync now", the time zone of the place (GeoJS) and by hand, the clock
    by hand and the hardware clock mode (eduka_datetime.py, timedatectl).
    A polkit rule lets people at the computer switch network time on and
    administrators change the time zone without a password; setting the
    clock by hand still asks for it.
  * LightDM: Edukasaun themes for slick-greeter and lightdm-gtk-greeter in
    the four styles of the SDDM login screen (Edukasaun-Login GTK themes,
    gradient backgrounds, logo), configured together in Eduka-Settings →
    Login & Fingerprint → LightDM: greeter, style, accent, clock,
    background, logo, "same look as SDDM", hidden account list, typing a
    name, guest account, automatic login and the display manager used at
    the next start. Root helper eduka-lightdm-apply with polkit actions;
    the live account is hidden for LightDM as well.
  * Accessibility rebuilt as Vision, Hearing and Screen Reader: large
    text, pointer size, reduce motion, magnifier and on-screen keyboard;
    status as text and mono sound (made again at every login); Orca with
    a voice setting (speed, pitch, volume, language, try it) and the keys
    to know. Eduka-Desktop tiles tell the screen reader what a program is
    for.
  * Parental Control: neater cards, recommendations by age (WHO and the
    Canadian 24-Hour Movement Guidelines), tips and a break reminder that
    Eduka-Panel shows. Privacy (new): recent files, thumbnails, trash.
  * Eduka-Quick (new): a round quick launcher inspired by Gnome-Pie by
    Simon Schneegans, drawn by the Eduka-Desktop daemon (Super+Q, command
    eduka-quick), with groups, keyboard use, animations, a round window
    without a compositor and its own settings page.
  * Fixes: tab labels with "&" lost a letter; the time zone is read from
    /etc/localtime first (systemd does not update /etc/timezone).
  * Packaging: recommends accountsservice and systemd-timesyncd |
    time-daemon; suggests the LightDM greeters, magnus and gufw; manual
    page for eduka-quick; translations for Portuguese, Indonesian and
    Tetun.

 -- Edukasaun OS <dev@edukasaun.org>  Wed, 11 Nov 2026 07:32:44 +0000

edukasaun-desktop-menu (0.11.0~rc1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Release candidate 0.11 RC of the final stable version.
  * Login: lxqt-panel, lxqt-notificationd and picom's own autostart entry
    stay off in Eduka-Desktop sessions (LXQt autostart entries with
    Hidden=true, written by the new eduka-session-prepare before LXQt
    starts and removed again with the package): no lxqt-panel flash at
    login, no second notification server, and only the picom Eduka starts
    runs, with Eduka's compositor settings (never twice). The Super key
    opens Eduka-Desktop (lxqt-globalkeys); a new account gets an Edukasaun
    wallpaper at its first login. Tested with a real LXQt session with
    xfwm4 and with Openbox and picom.
  * Official Edukasaun OS logo: the start button shows the logo and MENU
    (the old default label and picture change once), the menu header shows
    the Edukasaun OS wordmark and opens www.edukasaunos.tl; login screen,
    icons and About updated. System information: "Based on Debian
    Stable", no code name.
  * Eduka-Settings: pages about the same thing share one entry with tabs
    (17 entries became 11; old page names still work); new Touch Screen
    page (on/off, the monitor it belongs to, direction correction, kinetic
    finger scrolling, bigger buttons, Onboard on-screen keyboard) and
    Fingerprint page (fprintd; fingerprint login through pam-auth-update
    and a new polkit action). Row titles are translated; windows open
    centered with the title bar on the screen (it was above the screen
    with Openbox).
  * Menu: Edukasaun is the one category for learning, science and games;
    category name overrides match whole words; clearer empty category text;
    a short fade when it opens. Edukasaun-Dark: a nearly solid surface.
  * Wallpapers from /usr/share/background/Edukasaun (older folders are
    still read, chosen pictures keep working).
  * X11 and Wayland: input settings only in X11 sessions, a Wayland
    compositor is preselected for the test Wayland session, Firefox gets
    XInput 2, the touch screen is mapped again after screen changes.
  * Bug fix: a popup closed during its fade no longer raises an error.
  * The Timor Aid dictionary note is removed from the documents.
  * Recommends lxqt-globalkeys, fprintd, libpam-fprintd and onboard.
  * Translations (Portuguese, Indonesian, Tetun) of the new texts.
  * Details: /usr/share/edukasaun-desktop/doc/HISTORY.txt

 -- Edukasaun OS <dev@edukasaun.org>  Tue, 10 Nov 2026 06:17:14 +0000

edukasaun-desktop-menu (0.10.0~beta3) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Licenses: GPL-3.0-or-later with SPDX lines, a LICENSE file and a
    machine-readable copyright file listing every third-party part (Orchis,
    Graphite, Yaru-remix, Noto Emoji, Natural Earth); more credits in About.
  * Packaging: Debian changelog, manual pages for all commands, conffiles for
    the files in /etc, dh-style systemd handling; the package scripts no
    longer kill running programs, start programs as root or write into home
    folders. lintian: no errors or warnings.
  * Dependencies for Debian 13 (libqt5svg5, lxqt-session, dbus-bin, X11
    tools); the unused python3-xdg is dropped.
  * Autostart entries are LXQt modules (X-LXQt-Module, TryExec,
    --autostart); outside Eduka-Desktop sessions LXQt keeps its own panel
    and notifications. Eduka-Panel and Eduka-Desktop restart themselves
    after a package update.
  * Automatic login has its own polkit action that always asks for an
    administrator password; the login screen helper copies pictures safely.
  * Openbox: the theme goes to the file Openbox really reads; xfwm4: no
    square shadow around Eduka-Panel.
  * Liquid Glass: Action Center and popups in the theme blue, readable glass
    over dark wallpapers; readable "Action Center" label; deeper text
    shadow on the light login screen styles.
  * Light themes use Papirus-Light: dark Wi-Fi, sound and battery icons on
    the light panel (plain Papirus drew them light grey).
  * Bug fixes: Close on the task bar no longer kills windows, the menu no
    longer opens by itself, XDG-correct application list started without a
    shell, task bar names, several wired ports, LUKS/LVM system disks,
    weather switch, battery detection, eduka-panel-reset keeps a backup.
  * Translations (Portuguese, Indonesian, Tetun) of the new texts.
  * Details: /usr/share/edukasaun-desktop/doc/HISTORY.txt

 -- Edukasaun OS <dev@edukasaun.org>  Tue, 27 Oct 2026 02:35:16 +0000

